## 1️⃣ Control Panel vs Settings — Technician Mental Model

### Core Distinction
- **Settings**
  - Modern, user-facing
  - Permissions, apps, accounts
  - First stop for basic configuration
- **Control Panel**
  - Legacy but critical
  - Hardware, drivers, advanced troubleshooting
  - Preferred for diagnostics and repair

**Rule:**
> If it sounds technical or repair-oriented, start with Control Panel.

---

### High-Yield Control Panel Tools Reviewed
- **Devices and Printers** — peripherals, printers
- **Programs and Features** — uninstall/repair desktop apps
- **System** — OS version, hardware, activation
- **Network and Sharing Center** — adapter status (legacy)
- **Windows Defender Firewall** — inbound/outbound rules
- **Sound** — default playback/recording devices
- **Device Manager** — drivers, yellow warning triangles
- **Indexing Options** — broken Windows Search
- **Administrative Tools**
  - Event Viewer
  - Computer Management
- **File Explorer Options** — show extensions, hidden files
- **Power Options** — sleep, lid close behavior

---

### Key Settings Areas Reviewed
- **Apps** — uninstall Store apps, default apps
- **Network & Internet** — connection status, adapter config
- **Privacy** — camera/microphone permissions
- **Devices** — mouse, keyboard, basic printer setup
- **Accounts** — local vs Microsoft users
- **Gaming** — Game Mode, Game Bar
- **Update & Security** — updates, recovery

